  "summary": "Namespace deletion can bypass network policies in k8s.io/kubernetes",
  "details": "During namespace termination, network policy resources can be deleted before the Pods they protect, allowing the remaining Pods to bypass those policies.\n\nOrderedNamespaceDeletion is enabled by default in Kubernetes 1.33 and became GA in 1.34. Earlier releases still retain a feature gate whose behavior can follow an older emulated version. Kubernetes 1.37 removes that gate and unconditionally deletes Pods and waits for their termination before deleting other namespace resources.",
